- op: discuss  # fa91
  at: '2026-08-26T06:29:06Z'  # fa91
  by: agent  # fa91
  actor: jgstern_agent  # fa91
  clock: 3  # fa91
  nonce: fa91  # fa91
  message: "SATISFIED, and the item's framing was too narrow -- there are THREE facts under\nddg_mixed, not two, and the third dominates.\n\nThe filing names walk-returned-False vs walk-returned-None. Re-derived at the\ncall site, EVERY guard above the walk can fail with fn_has_ddg still true\n(sink_node != source_fn, no source call lines, no sink call lines, source not\ntracked, sink lexically before source) and the finding is stamped ddg_mixed\nanyway. So ddg_mixed means \"the DDG covered the function\", NOT \"the walk looked\nand found nothing\".\n\nFIX SHAPE CHOSEN, and why it is not one of the three the item listed as open.\nA NEW FIELD (TaintFlowFinding.walk_verdict), not a fourth analysis_method value.\nThe precedent the item cites -- splitting structural out of ddg_mixed -- separated\ntwo different ANALYSES. This separates one analysis's RESULTS, a different axis,\nand folding a verdict into a method name repeats the one-name-two-facts shape\nbeing fixed. It would also silently invalidate every published use of ddg_mixed\n(docs/measurements/0006, docs/VERIFY-CLAIMS-SCOPE.md). analysis_method's\nvocabulary is UNCHANGED and method_for_walk_verdict derives it from the verdict\nso the coarse and fine names cannot drift.\n\n  walk_verdict:    confirmed | unconfirmed | escaped | not_attempted | unavailable\n  walk_blocked_by: the FIRST guard that stopped a not_attempted walk\n\nBoth reach the verify-claims JSON evidence rows, which is what makes the domain\nmeasurable rather than upper-boundable. CONFIRM-ONLY IS UNCHANGED: nothing is\nacted on and no verdict moves.\n\nMEASURED IMMEDIATELY (docs/measurements/0007), census over the 11 of 0006's 16\nrepositories that carry a ddg_mixed finding, 298 evidence rows, no verdict hit\nthe 100-row evidence cap:\n\n  confirmed 14 | unconfirmed 0 | escaped 14 | not_attempted 139 | unavailable 131\n\n  ddg_mixed = 153 rows -> 0 unconfirmed / 14 escaped (9.2%) / 139 not_attempted\n  (90.8%). unconfirmed is ZERO IN EVERY REPOSITORY, not merely in aggregate.\n\nControl on the instrument: walk_blocked_by was added after a first pass and the\nwhole cohort re-run; the verdict table is byte-identical across both runs.\n\nINV-lupav L2 FIRED ON THE FIRST CUT, and it was right. Its contract test asserts\nthat a site which CONSUMES the walk's False must pass forfeit_refutation; a site\nthat COLLAPSES it with `is True` need not. This site used to collapse and now\nconsumes, because walk_verdict distinguishes unconfirmed from escaped -- so an\nUNEARNED False would have been published as \"the walk looked everywhere and\nfound nothing\", exactly the claim INV-lupav says is not earned. Gate wired in\nthe same change, as the guard's own docstring instructed. Third corpus arm with\nthe gate on: byte-identical to the ungated run, per repo and in total (expected,\nsince a forfeit can only move unconfirmed -> escaped and unconfirmed was 0).\n\nAlso: `no_sink_call_line` counts ZERO across the corpus but is REACHABLE, and is\ntested directly rather than pragma'd -- call_lines is populated only `if sites:`\nand _edge_call_sites yields nothing for an edge with no int line and no\nmeta['call_lines'], so a sink caller can exist with no recorded call line.\n\nMERGED: PR #542 (dev 1297c316a4 + 2fca492700)."  # fa91
